{"type":"after","callId":"call@288","endTime":507464.821,"result":{"matches":true,"received":{"value":{"s":"hidden"},"ariaSnapshot":"- link \"Skip to interactive specimen\":\n  - /url: \"#diss-canvas\"\n- link \"Skip to structure directory and notes\":\n  - /url: \"#diss-structure-directory\"\n- status: Progress saved locally on this device.\n- region \"Virtual Dissection Lab\":\n  - paragraph: Virtual Biology Laboratory\n  - heading \"Virtual Dissection Lab\" [level=2]\n  - paragraph: \"Work through the specimen one clear action at a time. Current focus: Study tools.\"\n  - list \"Dissection workflow\":\n    - listitem: Orient\n    - listitem: Prepare\n    - listitem: Reveal\n    - listitem: Identify\n    - listitem: Record evidence\n    - listitem: Review\n  - paragraph: Virtual practice supports observation and comparison. Follow your instructor’s safety, ethics, handling, and disposal procedures for any physical specimen.\n  - navigation \"Lab workspace shortcuts\":\n    - button \"Go to specimen\"\n    - button \"Structures and notes\"\n    - button \"Continue activity\"\n  - text: Specimen 🐸 Frog (Rana) Layer 3 of 5 · Organs Structures viewed 1 of 37\n- region \"Review the current structure flashcard\":\n  - text: Step 6 of 6 Next best action · Study tools\n  - heading \"Review the current structure flashcard\" [level=3]\n  - paragraph: Recall the function, compare your answer, and revisit the cards you mark for review.\n  - text: 🐸 Frog (Rana) 🫁 Organs · layer 3/5\n  - button \"Go to flashcards\"\n  - button \"View specimen\"\n- toolbar \"Learning route\":\n  - button \"Procedure practice\": 🔎 Procedure practice\n  - button \"Guided investigation\": 🧭 Guided investigation\n  - button \"Study tools\" [pressed]: 📚 Study tools\n  - button \"Practice assessment\": 🧠 Practice assessment\n  - group \"Workspace detail\":\n    - button \"Essentials workspace\" [pressed]: Essentials\n    - button \"Advanced workspace\": Advanced\n- region \"Choose a specimen\":\n  - heading \"Choose a specimen\" [level=3]\n  - paragraph: 7 comparative anatomy models\n  - tablist \"Dissection specimens\":\n    - 'tab \"Select specimen: Frog (Rana)\" [selected]': 🐸 Frog (Rana)\n    - 'tab \"Select specimen: Earthworm (Lumbricus)\"': 🪱 Earthworm (Lumbricus)\n    - 'tab \"Select specimen: Fetal Pig (Sus scrofa)\"': 🐷 Fetal Pig (Sus scrofa)\n    - 'tab \"Select specimen: Perch (Perca)\"': 🐟 Perch (Perca)\n    - 'tab \"Select specimen: Crayfish (Cambarus)\"': 🦞 Crayfish (Cambarus)\n    - 'tab \"Select specimen: Sheep Eye\"': 👁️ Sheep Eye\n    - 'tab \"Select specimen: Sheep Heart\"': ❤️ Sheep Heart\n- navigation \"Anatomical layers\":\n  - heading \"Anatomical layers\" [level=3]\n  - paragraph: 0 of 5 completed\n  - toolbar \"Specimen display and lab tool controls\":\n    - button \"View and accessibility options\": 👁 View & access ▼\n  - 'button \"Layer 1: Skin, available\"': 🟢 Skin\n  - 'button \"Layer 2: Muscle, available\"': 💪 Muscle\n  - 'button \"Layer 3: Organs, current\"': 🫁 Organs\n  - 'button \"Layer 4: Skeleton, locked\" [disabled]': 🦴 Skeleton\n  - 'button \"Layer 5: Nervous, locked\" [disabled]': ⚡ Nervous\n- region \"Study tools\":\n  - button \"Flashcard\" [pressed]: 🃏 Flashcard\n  - button \"Compare\": 🔍 Compare\n- 'tabpanel \"Select specimen: Frog (Rana)\"':\n  - region \"🐸 Frog (Rana) · Organs\":\n    - text: Interactive specimen\n    - heading \"🐸 Frog (Rana) · Organs\" [level=3]\n    - text: Limited observation field · 43%\n    - group:\n      - strong: View & orientation\n      - text: Internal · Organs +\n    - 'group \"Current action: Review the current structure flashcard. Study tools. Workflow step 6 of 6\"':\n      - strong: Next · Review the current structure flashcard\n      - text: Study tools Workflow 6/6\n    - group:\n      - strong: Field monitor\n      - text: Limited observation field Exposure and tissue-response details\n    - 'group \"Current pointer mode: Prediction required. Complete the prediction checkpoint before this instrument can contact the specimen.\"':\n      - strong: Pointer mode ? Prediction required\n      - text: Complete the prediction checkpoint before this instrument can contact the specimen.\n    - text: Frog (Rana) interactive specimen · Organs layer, internal view\n    - region \"Specimen canvas description\":\n      - heading \"Specimen canvas description\" [level=4]\n      - paragraph: Every canvas selection and drag action has a keyboard or button alternative. Use the structure directory for equivalent anatomical descriptions, the technique action button instead of drawing a stroke, the pin action button instead of dragging a pin, the probe action button instead of tracing a structure, and the pan controls instead of dragging a zoomed view. When the depth atlas is enabled, surface landmarks use circles, mid-depth landmarks use diamonds, and deep landmarks use double rings.\n      - paragraph: \"Frog (Rana) virtual dissection. Specimen-specific procedure: Frog ventral midline access; recommended view ventral; access route shallow ventral midline corridor; protected landmarks Heart (3-chamber), Liver (3 lobes), Lungs. Current view: internal, standard condition, Organs layer. Progressive exposure: Covered anatomy, 22 percent; decision quality 47 percent. Observation field: Limited observation field, 43 percent; limiting factor: Access width. Surface model: moist chromatophore surface. Surface microtexture uses chromatophores detail aligned to overhead illumination, with sheen adjusted for 72 percent moisture and standard condition. Tool contact response: elastic skin. Light direction: overhead. Illumination 68 percent: Balanced illumination; glare risk 6 percent. Focus isolation on. Tissue relief on and responsive to the inspection light. Depth atlas off. Selected and hovered structures use a labeled depth footprint with front and back edges, visibility-specific line styles, and boundary-attached relationship paths. Relationship types use distinct line patterns and moving marker shapes, with fixed markers when motion is reduced. Tubular, lobed, chambered, layered, and compact structure classes use distinct contours, internal patterns, and text labels. Anatomical orientation axis uses a circle for anterior and a diamond for posterior; current and target views are stated in text. View and layer navigation uses a labeled orientation sweep with circle start and diamond target markers, plus concentric depth rings for deeper or superficial movement; reduced motion switches instantly and uses text announcements. Depth motion off. 0 directly visible structures. Active instrument: probe. Action readiness: Prediction required, 70 percent. Complete the prediction checkpoint before this instrument can contact the specimen.. Directional contact footprint feedback is active. Engaged instrument tips use foreground tissue lips and paired depth notches to show partial insertion and opening-edge occlusion. Guided anatomical access corridor active; circle marks start and diamond marks finish. Directional target guidance uses a dashed arrow, labeled endpoint, and shape-coded reticle when an instrument is spatially misaligned. Localized action outcomes use a one-shot check or warning symbol with the changed tissue metric. Tissue opening, retraction, stabilization, hydration, and risk metrics transition spatially after each action; Undo reverses openings, retraction, pin placement, hydration, wick evidence, and probe traces; reduced motion snaps to the final state. Three-dimensional instrument pitch feedback is active. Light-aware instrument elevation feedback is active. Equivalent keyboard and button actions include an instrument approach, contact, and release replay. Recorded attempt replay progressively traces pressure with line width and states path alignment in text and shape. Direct forceps press-drag-release manipulation shows live lift direction, safe range, calibrated grip, speed, control, slip risk, and excess tension with text and geometry; the technique action button remains equivalent. Live pin stability preview shows endpoint spacing, calibrated angle, insertion depth, and flap tension with text and geometry. Direct pin press-drag-release placement adds shaft alignment, insertion travel, safe depth, and control feedback. Live probe palpation preview shows calibrated pressure, material resistance, anatomical depth, and tissue deformation with text and shape. Direct probe press-drag-release tracing adds contact coverage, alignment, resistance, deformation, and control feedback. Direct dropper press-drag-release hydration adds contact coverage, flow alignment, moisture, dose, and pooling feedback. Direct wick press-drag-release recovery adds pool-edge alignment, contact coverage, recovery distance, and control feedback. Live dropper spread forecast shows dose count, organism-specific flow direction, current saturation, and pooling risk with text and geometry. Absorbent-wick feedback shows pool-edge targeting, fluid recovery, and a localized balanced-film marker with text and cross-hatched geometry. Guided procedure handoff cue connects the next required instrument to its anatomical target and 6-step progress rail with text, shape, and line style. Persistent localized technique evidence maps edge stress, grip compression, anchor tension, probe pressure, and saline pooling to actual contact locations with text and distinct geometry; direct wick recovery maps pool-edge contact, recovery distance, and control. Press a visible structure, trace a short path while monitoring pressure, resistance, and contact, then release when controlled; the equivalent technique action button remains available. Occluded structures remain available in the structure directory.\"\n    - application \"Frog (Rana) interactive specimen · Organs layer, internal view\"\n    - button \"Zoom out canvas\": ➖\n    - text: 100%\n    - button \"Zoom in canvas\": ➕\n    - paragraph: Every canvas action has a keyboard or button alternative. The specimen canvas description lists them.\n    - status: \"Study tools: Review the current structure flashcard. Recall the function, compare your answer, and revisit the cards you mark for review.\"\n    - group: Evidence notebook · 0/6 frames\n    - group \"Technique practice · step 1 of 6\":\n      - strong: Technique controls\n      - text: Inspect ventral landmarks and confirm symmetry\n  - region \"Structure flashcards\":\n    - text: Reference practice · Frog (Rana)\n    - heading \"Structure flashcards\" [level=3]\n    - paragraph: Organs · All structures\n    - text: 1 / 12\n    - paragraph: Practice is separate from observed evidence and assessment scores. Drafts and self-ratings last for this activity; opening flashcards again or changing layers starts fresh.\n    - term: Recalled\n    - definition: \"0\"\n    - term: Review again\n    - definition: \"1\"\n    - term: Not rated\n    - definition: \"11\"\n    - text: 1 · Recall before revealing\n    - heading \"Heart (3-chamber)\" [level=4]\n    - paragraph: What does this structure do? Explain its main role in your own words. Say, sign, sketch, or write your answer.\n    - text: My recall draft (optional)\n    - textbox \"My recall draft (optional)\": It pumps blood around the body.\n    - button \"Reveal function Tap or press Enter to reveal its function\":\n      - strong: Reveal function\n      - text: Tap or press Enter to reveal its function\n    - button \"Previous flashcard\" [disabled]: Previous\n    - button \"Next without rating\"\n    - button \"Return to specimen\"\n  - complementary \"Structure directory and lab notes\":\n    - link \"Return to interactive specimen\":\n      - /url: \"#diss-canvas\"\n    - region \"🫁 Organs structures (12)\":\n      - heading \"🫁 Organs structures (12)\" [level=3]\n      - textbox \"Search organs in this layer\":\n        - /placeholder: Search names or functions…\n      - group \"Filter structures by learning progress\":\n        - button \"All structures, 12 structures\" [pressed]: All structures 12\n        - button \"To inspect, 11 structures\": To inspect 11\n        - button \"Needs notes, 0 structures\": Needs notes 0\n        - button \"Recorded, 1 structures\": Recorded 1\n      - paragraph: Filters apply to this layer. Recorded means a note and confidence are present, not verified mastery.\n      - status: 12 structures available in Organs.\n      - region \"Directory results\":\n        - button \"Heart (3-chamber), previously viewed; review evidence\": Heart (3-chamber) Note and confidence recorded Prior evidence\n        - button \"Lungs, not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Lungs Not yet inspected Not visible\n        - button \"Liver (3 lobes), not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Liver (3 lobes) Not yet inspected Not visible\n        - button \"Gallbladder, not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Gallbladder Not yet inspected Not visible\n        - button \"Stomach, not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Stomach Not yet inspected Not visible\n        - button \"Small Intestine, not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Small Intestine Not yet inspected Not visible\n        - button \"Large Intestine, not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Large Intestine Not yet inspected Not visible\n        - button \"Spleen, not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Spleen Not yet inspected Not visible\n        - button \"Kidneys, not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Kidneys Not yet inspected Not visible\n        - button \"Fat Bodies, not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Fat Bodies Not yet inspected Not visible\n        - button \"Pancreas, not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Pancreas Not yet inspected Not visible\n        - button \"Cloaca, not currently visible; preview only\" [disabled]: Cloaca Not yet inspected Not visible\n    - text: Layer Progress 🟢 Skin 💪 Muscle 🫁 Organs 🦴 Skeleton ⚡ Nervous\n    - paragraph: Classic vertebrate — 3-chambered heart, cutaneous respiration, metamorphosis.\n    - paragraph: \"Comparative learning model: specimen observations and human clinical connections are labeled separately. Anatomy varies by species, age, preservation, and individual.\"\n    - group: Biology fact ＋\n    - text: 📊 Learning evidence 3%\n    - 'progressbar \"Observation: structures viewed 1 of 37\"'\n    - text: \"Observation: 1 of 37 structures viewed Technique 0%\"\n    - progressbar \"Technique evidence\"\n    - text: Observation 3%\n    - progressbar \"Observation evidence\"\n    - text: Evidence 3%\n    - progressbar \"Evidence evidence\"\n    - text: Understanding 6%\n    - progressbar \"Understanding evidence\"\n    - text: 0/2 guided identifications verified · 1/37 evidence records · completed first-attempt assessment 0/0\n    - button \"Review 1 missed structure\"\n    - text: Practice in progress Continue the investigation; the log distinguishes viewing from verified understanding.\n    - button \"Copy practice log to clipboard\": Copy practice log\n    - group: Specimen stats ＋\n    - group: Learning objectives ＋\n    - group: Key terms ＋\n- status"}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@288"}
